is silent, only the spelling moves","homophoneKey":"vizit"},{"id":"fr:visité","languageId":"fr","surface":"visité","gloss":"visited","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m15","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"vee-zee-TAY — the past participle; a pure written-only homophone of «visiter» itself — see the module header"},{"id":"fr:halle","languageId":"fr","surface":"halle","gloss":"covered market","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m15","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"al — h ASPIRÉ: «la halle», never «l'halle», unlike m4's «l'hôtel»","gender":"f","hAspire":true},{"id":"fr:aller","languageId":"fr","surface":"aller","gloss":"to go","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"ah-LAY — bare infinitive; sounds IDENTICAL to its own participle «allé» (regular -er→-é, same as manger/mangé, visiter/visité) — no homophoneKey needed, that machinery pairs one word's own forms, not two different words; see the module header for the bespoke test pin instead"},{"id":"fr:allé","languageId":"fr","surface":"allé","gloss":"went / gone (m)","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"ah-LAY — past participle, masculine; [ale] either way against «allée» — the course's first SILENT gender pair, never graded by ear","homophoneKey":"ale"},{"id":"fr:allée","languageId":"fr","surface":"allée","gloss":"went / gone (f)","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"same sound as «allé» — only the spelling agrees with a feminine subject","homophoneKey":"ale"},{"id":"fr:venir","languageId":"fr","surface":"venir","gloss":"to come","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"vuh-NEER — bare infinitive; a genuinely new verb, no present-tense chunk to lean on (unlike aller's je vais / tu vas / on va)"},{"id":"fr:venu","languageId":"fr","surface":"venu","gloss":"came (m)","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"vuh-NU — IRREGULAR participle, not the -ir→-i pattern; does NOT rhyme with «venir»","homophoneKey":"vəny"},{"id":"fr:venue","languageId":"fr","surface":"venue","gloss":"came (f)","partOfSpeech":"verb","fromModule":"m16","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"same sound as «venu» — [vəny] either way; the module's second silent gender pair","homophoneKey":"vəny"},{"id":"fr:onze","languageId":"fr","surface":"onze","gloss":"eleven","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"ohnz — starts like a consonant, same class as «huit»: say «le onze», never «l'onze»","consonantOnset":true},{"id":"fr:douze","languageId":"fr","surface":"douze","gloss":"twelve","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"dooz"},{"id":"fr:treize","languageId":"fr","surface":"treize","gloss":"thirteen","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"trehz"},{"id":"fr:quatorze","languageId":"fr","surface":"quatorze","gloss":"fourteen","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"ka-TORZ"},{"id":"fr:quinze","languageId":"fr","surface":"quinze","gloss":"fifteen","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"kanz"},{"id":"fr:seize","languageId":"fr","surface":"seize","gloss":"sixteen","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"sehz — not to be confused with «seize» the English verb, pure coincidence of spelling"},{"id":"fr:quatre-vingts","languageId":"fr","surface":"quatre-vingts","gloss":"eighty (exactly)","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m17","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"kat-ruh-VAN — «quatre» × «vingt», four twenties; the trailing -s shows ONLY when nothing follows (quatre-vingts alone) and disappears the instant a unit joins (quatre-vingt-un)"},{"id":"fr:jamais","languageId":"fr","surface":"jamais","gloss":"never (with ne)","partOfSpeech":"adverb","fromModule":"m18","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🚫","hint":"zha-MEH — pairs with «ne» exactly like «pas»: «ne ... jamais» = never. It contains «mais» (but) as a written substring — say the whole word, don't clip it."},{"id":"fr:rien","languageId":"fr","surface":"rien","gloss":"nothing (with ne)","partOfSpeech":"pronoun","fromModule":"m18","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🕳️","hint":"ryan — pairs with «ne» exactly like «pas»: «ne ... rien» = nothing. Sounds close to «bien» (well) — lean on the sentence around it, not the sound alone."},{"id":"fr:il va","languageId":"fr","surface":"il va","gloss":"he's going / he's going to","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m19","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"eel VAH — same «aller» engine as «je vais/tu vas/on va», third person"},{"id":"fr:elle va","languageId":"fr","surface":"elle va","gloss":"she's going / she's going to","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m19","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"ell VAH — same engine, feminine subject"},{"id":"fr:je viens de","languageId":"fr","surface":"je viens de","gloss":"I just (have just)","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m20","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"zhuh vyeh(n) duh — «venir» present tense + de, fronting a verb = recent past"},{"id":"fr:tu viens de","languageId":"fr","surface":"tu viens de","gloss":"you just (have just)","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m20","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"tu vyeh(n) duh — same «viens» as «je viens de», different subject"},{"id":"fr:il vient de","languageId":"fr","surface":"il vient de","gloss":"he just (has just)","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m20","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"eel vyeh(n) duh — third person, same engine as m19's «il va»"},{"id":"fr:elle vient de","languageId":"fr","surface":"elle vient de","gloss":"she just (has just)","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m20","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"ell vyeh(n) duh — third person, feminine subject"},{"id":"fr:cents","languageId":"fr","surface":"cents","gloss":"hundred(s) — plural of «cent»","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m21","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"sahn — same sound as «cent», the -s is silent; it shows in writing ONLY when a multiplier (deux, trois...) precedes it AND nothing follows — deux cents, but deux cent un"},{"id":"fr:mille","languageId":"fr","surface":"mille","gloss":"one thousand","partOfSpeech":"other","fromModule":"m21","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"meel — the next round ceiling after «cent»; UNLIKE «cent», it never takes -s, at any size: mille, deux mille, trois mille..."},{"id":"fr:sac","languageId":"fr","surface":"sac","gloss":"bag","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m22","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🎒","hint":"sak — unlike «chat», the c IS pronounced here","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:heure","languageId":"fr","surface":"heure","gloss":"hour / o'clock","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m23","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🕐","hint":"ur — feminine: UNE heure, not UN heure","gender":"f","homophoneKey":"œʁ"},{"id":"fr:heures","languageId":"fr","surface":"heures","gloss":"hours / o'clock (plural)","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m23","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"same sound as «heure» — the plural -s is silent","gender":"f","homophoneKey":"œʁ"},{"id":"fr:jus","languageId":"fr","surface":"jus","gloss":"juice","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🧃","hint":"zhoo — blue-m","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:pomme","languageId":"fr","surface":"pomme","gloss":"apple","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🍎","hint":"pum — pink-f","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:baguette","languageId":"fr","surface":"baguette","gloss":"baguette (bread)","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🥖","hint":"ba-GET — pink-f","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:tarte","languageId":"fr","surface":"tarte","gloss":"pie / tart","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🥧","hint":"tart — pink-f","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:crêpe","languageId":"fr","surface":"crêpe","gloss":"crêpe","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🥞","hint":"krehp — pink-f","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:soupe","languageId":"fr","surface":"soupe","gloss":"soup","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🍲","hint":"soop — pink-f","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:ouvert","languageId":"fr","surface":"ouvert","gloss":"open (m-form)","partOfSpeech":"adjective","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"oo-VEHR — the t sleeps"},{"id":"fr:ouverte","languageId":"fr","surface":"ouverte","gloss":"open (f-form)","partOfSpeech":"adjective","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"oo-VEHRT — the -e wakes the t, the grand/grande trick again"},{"id":"fr:fermé","languageId":"fr","surface":"fermé","gloss":"closed (m-form)","partOfSpeech":"adjective","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"fehr-MAY","homophoneKey":"fɛʁme"},{"id":"fr:fermée","languageId":"fr","surface":"fermée","gloss":"closed (f-form)","partOfSpeech":"adjective","fromModule":"m24","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","hint":"fehr-MAY — sounds IDENTICAL to fermé; the -e is silent here","homophoneKey":"fɛʁme"},{"id":"fr:c'est qui ?","languageId":"fr","surface":"c'est qui ?","gloss":"who is it? / who's that?","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m25","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"say KEE — the same end-of-sentence question slot as «tu vas où ?» and «il est quelle heure ?»"},{"id":"fr:qui est-ce ?","languageId":"fr","surface":"qui est-ce ?","gloss":"who is it? (written / fronted)","partOfSpeech":"phrase","fromModule":"m25","srsEligible":true,"kind":"phrase","hint":"kee ES-suh — the fronted, written-register twin; recognize it, never asked to say it"},{"id":"fr:chambre","languageId":"fr","surface":"chambre","gloss":"bedroom","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🛏️","hint":"SHAHM-br — bedroom","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:salon","languageId":"fr","surface":"salon","gloss":"living room","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🛋️","hint":"sah-LOHN — nasal ending, living room","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:cuisine","languageId":"fr","surface":"cuisine","gloss":"kitchen","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🍳","hint":"kwee-ZEEN — kitchen","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:jardin","languageId":"fr","surface":"jardin","gloss":"garden / yard","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🌷","hint":"zhar-DAN — nasal ending, garden","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:lait","languageId":"fr","surface":"lait","gloss":"milk","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🥛","hint":"LAY — milk","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:eau","languageId":"fr","surface":"eau","gloss":"water","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"💧","hint":"OH — water; always heard as «l'eau», never bare","gender":"f"},{"id":"fr:pain","languageId":"fr","surface":"pain","gloss":"bread","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🍞","hint":"PAN — nasal ending, bread","gender":"m"},{"id":"fr:beurre","languageId":"fr","surface":"beurre","gloss":"butter","partOfSpeech":"noun","fromModule":"m26","srsEligible":true,"kind":"vocab","emoji":"🧈","hint":"BUHR — butter","gender":"m"}]